---
<BaseLayout
  title="Balls (Yes)"
  description="TODO: Write a short description for Balls (Yes)."
>
  <section class="la-page">
    <ProblemsSidebar />

    <article class="topic-article">
      <header class="topic-hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">Analysis · Problems</span>
        <h1>Balls (Yes)</h1>

        <p>
          TODO: Write a short introduction to this problem set.
        </p>
      </header>

      <nav class="topic-toc" aria-label="Problem rounds">
        <a href="#round-i">Round I</a>
        <a href="#round-ii">Round II</a>
        <a href="#round-iii">Round III</a>
        <a href="#round-iv">Round IV</a>
        <a href="#round-v">Round V</a>
      </nav>

      <section class="topic-section" id="round-i">
        <h2>Round I</h2>

        <Equation
          tex={String.raw`A = \{ (x_1, x_2) \in \R^2 : |x_1| + |x_2| \leq 1 \}.`}
        />

        <MathCanvas2D
          id="balls-yes-canvas"
          label="Placeholder visualization for Balls (Yes)."
          aspectRatio="16 / 9"
        />

        <details class="drop-example">
          <summary>Solution</summary>

          <div class="drop-content">
            <p>
	      We'll consider the special case that turns the inequality sign into an equality one:
            </p>

	    <Equation
              tex={String.raw`|x_1| + |x_2| = 1.`}
            />

	    <p>
	      First, observe that since <Math tex = "|x_1| = 1 - |x_2| \geq 0"/> and <Math tex = "|x_2| = 1 - |x_1| \geq 0"/>, it means
              both <Math tex = "x_1"/> and <Math tex = "x_2"/> lie between <Math tex = "0"/> and <Math tex = "1"/>.
            </p>

	    <p>
	      By considering all the relevant intervals, we can write <Math tex = "x_1"/> in terms of <Math tex = "x_2"/> like so:
	    </p>

	    <Equation
              tex={String.raw`
	      x_1 =
	      \left\{
	      \begin{array}{cc}
	      1 - x_2 & x_1 \geq 0, x_2 \geq 0\\
	      1 + x_2 & x_1 \geq 0, x_2 \leq 0\\
	      x_2 - 1 & x_1 \leq 0, x_2 \geq 0\\
	      -x_2 - 1 & x_1 \leq 0, x_2 \leq 0\\
	      \end{array}
	      \right..
              `}
            />

	    <p> These are all line equations: </p>
	      
	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`d_1: x_1 = 1 - x_2;`}
	    />

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`d_2: x_1 = 1 + x_2;`}
	    />

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`d_3: x_1 = x_2 - 1;`}
	    />

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`d_4: x_1 = -x_2 - 1.`}
	    />

	    <p> To be able to represent them graphically, we are going to find their respective axes intersection points: </p>

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`(1, 0), (0, 1) \in d_1;`}
	    />

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`(1, 0), (0, -1) \in d_2;`}
	    />

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`(-1, 0), (0, 1) \in d_3;`}
	    />

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`(-1, 0), (0, -1) \in d_4.`}
	    />

	    <MathCanvas2D
	      id="diamond_ball"
	      label="The set A represented geometrically."
	      aspectRatio="16 / 9"
	    />

	    
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>
      <section class="topic-section" id="round-ii">
        <h2>Round II</h2>

        <p>
          TODO: Add the exercises for Round II. You can use inline
          mathematics such as <Math tex="n \in \mathbb{N}" /> directly in the
          problem statement.
        </p>

         <Equation
          tex={String.raw`B = \{ (x_1, x_2) \in \R^2 : x_2 \geq |x_1|, x_2 \leq 2 \}.`}
        />

        <details class="drop-example">
          <summary>Solution</summary>

          <div class="drop-content">
	    <p> The restriction this time is:  <Math tex = "x_2 \geq |x_1| \geq 0"/>. </p>
	    
            <p>
	      Repeating the previous process, we end up with the lines:
            </p>

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`d_1: x_1 = x_2;`}
	    />

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`d_2: x_1 = -x_2;`}
	    />

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`d_3: x_2 = 2.`}
	    />

	    <MathCanvas2D
	      id="triangle_ball"
	      label="The set B represented geometrically."
	      aspectRatio="16 / 9"
	    />
	    
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>
      <section class="topic-section" id="round-iii">
        <h2>Round III</h2>

        <p>
          TODO: Add the exercises for Round III. You can use inline
          mathematics such as <Math tex="n \in \mathbb{N}" /> directly in the
          problem statement.
        </p>

        <Equation
          tex={String.raw`C = \{  (x_1, x_2) \in \mathbb{R}^2 : x_1^2 + x_2^2 \leq 3, x_1 \leq 2|x_2| \}.`}
        />

        <details class="drop-example">
          <summary>Solution</summary>

          <div class="drop-content">
            <p>
	      Since <Math tex = "x_1^2 + x_2^2 \leq 3"/>, the domain for both <Math tex = "x_1"/> and <Math tex = "x_2"/> is <Math tex = "[-\sqrt{3}, \sqrt{3}]"/>.
	      This particular equation is of course one of a circle of center <Math tex = "(0, 0)"/> and radius <Math tex = "\sqrt{3}"/>.
            </p>

	    <p> Considering the case of equality for the second inequation, we get: </p>

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`d_1: x_1 = 2x_2;`}
	    />

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`d_2: x_1 = -2x_2.`}
	    />

	    <p> We have to find the intersection points between the aforementioned circle and the two lines we've just find. </p>

	    <Equation
	      tex={String.raw`
	      \frac{1}{2}x_1 = \sqrt{3 - x_1^2}.
              `}
	    />

	    <p>
	      Solving this and the analogous second equation, we obtain the
              points <Math tex = "\left(\frac{2\sqrt{15}}{5}, \frac{\sqrt{15}}{5}\right)"/> and <Math tex = "\left(\frac{2\sqrt{15}}{5}, -\frac{\sqrt{15}}{5}\right)"/>
	      respectively.
	    </p>

	    
	    <MathCanvas2D
	      id="circle_sector_ball"
	      label="The set C represented geometrically."
	      aspectRatio="16 / 9"
	    />
	    
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>
